    rdfs:label "]\\\\ \\& |[schemanode]| encyclopediaApex tikzcd% Cross-page citation: the citation arrow commutes at the encyclopedia apex.fig:music-cross-page-references-compatibility theorem[Cross-page citation commutes] thm:music-cross-page-citation-commutes A cross-page citation arrow \\(cites:P1 P2\\) is admissible only when the triangle commutes at the encyclopedia apex. theorem proof Step 1 (legs). \\(1\\) and \\(2\\) are typed. Step 2 (citation). The citation arrow is the named cross-page reference. Step 3 (commutativity). The two paths agree at the apex. Step 4 (no false citation). A citation to a non-existent page fails commutativity. proof example[worked: Music cites paper 19's whole-as-colimit discipline] ex:music-cites-paper-19 Take \\(P1\\) = the Music entry (this paper); take \\(P2\\) = paper 19 (mereology-as-colimit). The citation arrow \\(cites:P1 P2\\) is implemented in chapters/12\\cross\\paper\\bridges/sections/06\\bridge\\to\\mereology\\as\\colimit.tex. The citation names the load-bearing claim" .
